 ## Overview
-Neural Scene Graphs (NSG) is a method for decomposing dynamic, multi-object scenes into a learned hierarchical scene graph with decoupled object transformations and scene representations [S1]. It solves the problem of novel view synthesis and rendering of unseen arrangements in dynamic scenes by lifting the assumption of static scene consistency required by existing neural rendering methods [S1]. Unlike methods that encode the entire scene into a single, static network, NSG uses a hierarchical scene-graph model with object-level implicit representations, allowing for the learning of object representations directly from video frames and tracking data [S1].
+Neural Scene Graphs (NSG) is a method for decomposing dynamic, multi-object scenes into a learned hierarchical scene graph with decoupled object transformations and scene representations [S2]. It solves the problem of novel view synthesis and rendering of unseen arrangements in dynamic scenes by lifting the assumption of static scene consistency required by existing neural rendering methods [S2]. Unlike methods that encode the entire scene into a single, static network, NSG uses a hierarchical scene-graph model with object-level implicit representations, allowing for the learning of object representations directly from video frames and tracking data [S2].
 
 ## How it works
